1. Array Questions to Prepare 
1. Second Largest & Second Smallest Element: Find without sorting in $O(N)$ time. 
2. Rotate Array by $K$ Positions: Clockwise (Right) and Anti-clockwise (Left). 
3. Find the Missing Number: Find missing element in range $[1, N]$. 
4. Find Leaders in Array: Elements greater than all elements on their right.  
5. Maximum Subarray Sum (Kadane's Algorithm): Handle both positive and negative arrays. 
6. Sort Array of 0s, 1s, and 2s: In single-pass $O(N)$ without sorting functions. 
7. Equilibrium Index: Find index where sum of lower indices equals sum of higher indices. 
8. Majority Element (Boyer-Moore Voting): Find element appearing more than $N/2$ times.  
9. Two Sum / Triplets with Zero Sum: Pair or triplet matching given target sum. 
10. Remove Duplicates: From sorted and unsorted arrays.  
2. String Questions to Prepare 
1. Anagram Check & Character Frequencies: Print frequencies in order of appearance.  
2. First Non-Repeating Character: Return first unique character or -1.  
3. Palindrome String & Word Reversal: Check palindrome; reverse words in a sentence.  
4. Longest Common Prefix: Find longest matching prefix across an array of strings.  
5. Count Vowels, Consonants, and Special Characters: Ignore spaces and format counts.  
6. Remove Spaces & Remove Duplicates: Clean string without extra string libraries. 
7. String Rotation Check: Determine if $S_2$ is a rotation of $S_1$.  
8. Longest Word in a Sentence: Extract the word with maximum length. 
3. Number Theory & Math Logic Questions 
Prepare single-function checks for all these number types: 
• Prime Number: Check single prime & print all primes in range $[A, B]$.  
• Armstrong Number: Sum of digits raised to power of digit-count equals the number. 
• Trailing Zeros in Factorial: $\lfloor N/5 \rfloor + \lfloor N/25 \rfloor + \dots$ without 
overflow. 
• Fibonacci Series: Nth term and series up to $N$ terms. 
4. Matrix & Pattern Questions (Advanced / Digital Track) 
1. Spiral Matrix Traversal: Traversal of $M \times N$ matrix layer-by-layer. 
2. Matrix Transpose & Diagonal Sum: Primary and secondary diagonal calculations.
